-- title:
--   The original actual single-section polynomial algebra and three-generator basis
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring. In the actual ordinary order-thirteen coordinate ring set $t=y+x^3+x^2+1$, $p=xt$ and $q=x(p+2)$, and let $R[T]$ act through $T\mapsto t$. The specified algebra is $B=R[T][p,q]$. If two is a unit, then $B$ is finite and its underlying module is the span of $1,p,q$. If $R$ is also an integral domain, the original constructor provides a basis with values $1,p,q$, so $B$ is free of rank three. This interface supplies the polynomial-algebra and basis data used by the actual finite free level sets and FiniteMapData.
-- source:
--   Selected original declarations from MazurTheorem Order13SingleSectionFiniteAlgebra.lean, Order13SingleSectionPolynomialCombinationIndependence.lean and Order13SingleSectionFiniteAlgebraBasis.lean. Every data constructor body is unchanged, including the original basis constructor. Three proof bodies instead consume the already Proved public finite-coordinate-algebra and basis theorems and structural subalgebra operations. All eighteen original types and every data value are kernel-compared with the retained original implementation, with closed universe parameters. Complete Lean frontend ranges select original declarations; per-file headers and Apache-2.0 are retained. Named downstream consumers are the actual finite free level sets and full FiniteMapData. Vas and contributors.

